    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14964" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dūrābĭlis</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		duro, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>lasting</i>, <i>durable</i> (rare; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">not ante-Aug.): quod caret alterna requie
					durabile non est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. H.
					4, 89</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Col. 12, 38, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">12, 55, 1</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vox,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 11, 3, 23 al.</span></i>
			—<i>Comp.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">durabilior materies,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Mag. p. 314, 13</span></i>
			.—<i>Sup.</i> does not
				occur.—<i>Adv.</i>: 
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dūrābĭlĭter</span></b> ,
				<i>in a lasting manner</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cassiod. Hist. Eccl. 1, 9</span></i>.</div>
